{
 "id": 79,
 "number": 51,
 "title": "N-Queens",
 "slug": "n-queens",
 "category": "backtracking",
 "difficulty": "Hard",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/n-queens/",
 "pattern": "Backtracking row by row with attack sets",
 "statement": "Place `n` queens on an `n × n` chessboard so that **no two queens attack each other** (no shared row, column or diagonal). Return every distinct solution; each solution is the board as a list of strings, `Q` for a queen and `.` for an empty square.",
 "example": {
  "input": "n = 4",
  "output": "[[\".Q..\",\"...Q\",\"Q...\",\"..Q.\"],[\"..Q.\",\"Q...\",\"...Q\",\".Q..\"]]",
  "why": "For a 4 × 4 board there are exactly two arrangements; they are mirror images of each other."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "n = 1",
   "output": "[[\"Q\"]]"
  },
  {
   "input": "n = 2",
   "output": "[]"
  },
  {
   "input": "n = 3",
   "output": "[]"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Every row needs exactly one queen, so place them **row by row**: for the current row, try each column.",
  "A square is safe if no earlier queen shares its column or a diagonal. Along a `\\` diagonal (top-left to bottom-right) `row − col` never changes; along a `/` diagonal (top-right to bottom-left) `row + col` never changes. Three sets remember which columns and diagonals are taken, so the check is O(1).",
  "Safe → place the queen and go to the next row. If a row has no safe square, go back, **remove** the previous queen and try its next column. Reaching row `n` means all queens are placed."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def solveNQueens(self, n: int) -> List[List[str]]:\n        cols = set()  # columns that already hold a queen\n        diag = set()  # (row - col) is constant along a \"\\\" diagonal\n        anti = set()  # (row + col) is constant along a \"/\" diagonal\n        board = [[\".\"] * n for _ in range(n)]\n        result = []\n\n        def place_queen(row):\n            if row == n:\n                result.append([\"\".join(line) for line in board])\n                return\n\n            for col in range(n):\n                if col in cols or (row - col) in diag or (row + col) in anti:\n                    continue  # this square is attacked\n\n                board[row][col] = \"Q\"\n                cols.add(col)\n                diag.add(row - col)\n                anti.add(row + col)\n\n                place_queen(row + 1)\n\n                board[row][col] = \".\"\n                cols.remove(col)\n                diag.remove(row - col)\n                anti.remove(row + col)\n\n        place_queen(0)\n        return result",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n!)",
  "timeWhy": "The first row has n choices, the next at most n − 1, and so on; the attack sets make each check O(1).",
  "space": "O(n²)",
  "spaceWhy": "The board is n × n; the sets and the recursion hold at most n entries (not counting the output)."
 },
